<BR>
It's one I got ready because <STYLE ID="3">Haruka</STYLE> asked to wear a Noh mask for the grave visit.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Apparently it's a Niimura family custom.<PG>
It's a little late, but today is the grave visit for the third-year memorial.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
This grave was built at the request of <STYLE ID="7">my mom</STYLE>, who was in the detention cell 2 years ago.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="8">Obasan</STYLE> is buried at a place called the Arata settlement, but apparently this kind of arrangement is called the two-grave system.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
So that when <STYLE ID="3">Haruka</STYLE> woke up, she could visit the grave easily even if her body wouldn't move freely.<PG>
<STYLE ID="3">Haruka</STYLE>, her real daughter, and <STYLE ID="8">Obasan</STYLE>, the one who raised her.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
<STYLE ID="7">My mom</STYLE>, who holds both of them dear, wanted to keep the <STYLE ID="9" RUBY="きずな">bond</STYLE> between those two tied together, and this is the last thing she left behind in the <STYLE ID="10" RUBY="しゃば">outside world</STYLE>.<PG>
<STYLE ID="3">Haruka</STYLE> recovered rapidly after that, but it still took time before she got permission to go out.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
The aftereffects of the anesthesia everyone had worried about gradually went away, and now she can talk freely.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Apparently, if she keeps up her rehab, she may even be able to walk.<PG>
