Long ago, there was a devout woman.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
But her mother-in-law didn't like that.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
The mother-in-law put on a mask and frightened the woman, but the mask bit into her heart and body.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Clutching at <STYLE ID="11" RUBY="わら">straws</STYLE>, the mother-in-law prayed, and she was able to take the mask off.<PG>
The flesh-bound mask―
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
A folk tale that teaches the importance of faith in the gods and the Buddha.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
I, too, had had this flesh-bound mask on.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
But unlike in the folk tale, I had been trying to fool my own heart by wearing the mask.<PG>
My body and heart had been screaming, yet I hid it by wearing the mask.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
At the same time, it was a sign that I didn't want my real face to be seen.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
A sign of a heart screaming for someone to help it.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
I couldn't say the one phrase 'help me.'
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Because that was my self-righteous atonement.<PG>
I have people who took that mask off me and led me out into a new world.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
What I saw beyond my widened view was a new world, shining more dazzlingly than ever before.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Alone―through self-righteous atonement, it was a world I could never have seen.<PG>
